==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Cooldown Equality}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*2 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[THE FOLIVOREAN]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
**6 [[Condemned Peng]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 40~46.67 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Abuse the startoff of this stage to stack [[Cyberpunk Cat]]s.

When you hit the base, you are met with THE FOLIVOREAN, Rajakong, and six Condemned Pengs aiming to nuke your stacks with their Death Surges. The double Behemoth combo is helpless against [[Cat Egg Pod]], UL Legends, and Behemoth Slayers like [[Mushroom Cat]] and [[Courier Cat]], while the Pengs get chipped to death from [[Jelly Dumpling Cat]] and the Cyberstack you built up earlier.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Backliners that outrange THE FOLIVOREAN: Examples include [[God-Emperor Daliasan]], [[King of Destiny Phonoa]], and [[Almighty Lucifer]].
*[[Cake Machine (Uber Rare Cat)|Wedding Cake Machine]]: Cake Machine is designed to be a tanker for Akus and Angels, which are the most prominent traits in this stage. As long as other units can keep the Doge Darks at bay, Cake Machine can survive for a long time against Rajakong and THE FOLIVOREAN.

